# KINETIC ENGINE CONFIGURATION: LOCAL-FIRST HUB & SPOKE GENERATOR
# Target: Oregon Exterior Experts CMS (Supabase)
# Inherits: blog-template.mdc (Founder voice, Topic Clusters, Oregon Reality filters, Linking Logic, Technical Constraints, Execution Order)

## [PROCEDURAL TASK]
Generate 7 Pillar Posts (Hubs) and their corresponding 21 Spoke Posts (Children) for the Topic Clusters defined in @.cursor/rules/blog-template.mdc

Each Hub must act as the ultimate authority on the topic, while Spokes target specific local/transactional intent.

## [FILE OUTPUT PROTOCOL]
Before generating any posts, read and follow: @.cursor/rules/blog-output-protocol.mdc

All generated posts MUST:
- Be routed to the correct cluster folder (cluster-1-moss-algae-prevention through cluster-7-home-exterior-health)
- Be placed in the phase2/ subfolder within each cluster
- Follow naming conventions: `pillar-{title-slug}.md` or `spoke-{title-slug}.md` (slug derived from `h1_title`, see output protocol)
- Use the cluster mapping and file routing rules defined in the output protocol

## [BATCH 0: CONTENT MANIFEST]
The Content Manifest schema template is at `blog/data/manifest.json`.

Read the JSON file. The following fields are pre-filled and locked — do NOT modify them:
`cluster`, `post_type`, `primary_keyword`, `h1_title`, `intent`, `parent_post`, `sibling_posts`

Complete ONLY fields set to `null`:
- `slug` — derive from `primary_keyword` + `target_city`
- `one_sentence_summary` — write using the `primary_keyword` in the Founder voice, shaped by the `intent` classification
- `target_neighborhood` — read `blog/data/neighborhood-matrix.json`, select a neighborhood from the array matching the post's `target_city`. Distribute neighborhoods across posts so no two posts in the same cluster share the same neighborhood.
- `target_landmark` — read `blog/data/landmark-matrix.json`, select a landmark from the array matching the post's `target_city`. Choose a landmark geographically near the chosen `target_neighborhood`. Distribute landmarks across posts so no two posts in the same cluster share the same landmark.

Do NOT modify any pre-filled fields. Write the completed manifest to `blog/data/completed/phase1.json` before proceeding to Batch 1.

## [BATCH 1: PILLAR POSTS]
Generate the 7 Parent Pillar Posts using the completed Content Manifest as a reference for all inline spoke links.
Format:
- H1: Use `h1_title` from the manifest
- Intent: Split `intent` on ` / `. Read `blog/data/intent-matrix.json`. Apply `primary_intents[primary]` as the base, then merge any `*_override` fields from `modifiers[modifier]`. Use the resolved `tone`, `cta_placement`, `content_depth`, and `structure` to shape the post.
- Body: Intro (Straight-talk) -> The Physics of the Problem -> The 2026 Code Solution -> The "Neighborhood" Spotlight. Spoke links are woven inline throughout — no dedicated link section. Use each Spoke's `one_sentence_summary` from the manifest as the teaser text.

## [BATCH 2: SPOKE POSTS]
Generate the 21 Spoke Posts using the completed Content Manifest as a reference for all parent and sibling links.
Format:
- H1: Use `h1_title` from the manifest
- Intent: Split `intent` on ` / `. Read `blog/data/intent-matrix.json`. Apply `primary_intents[primary]` as the base, then merge any `*_override` fields from `modifiers[modifier]`. Use the resolved `tone`, `cta_placement`, `content_depth`, and `structure` to shape the post.
- Body: Intro (Local problem framing) -> The Physics/Evidence -> The Code/Standard -> The Fix. Close with "The Bigger Picture" paragraph using `parent_post` and `sibling_posts` from the manifest.